      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\nAcetaminophen 2000 mg PO three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day. That is above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 2,000 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. At that daily total, the risk of hepatotoxicity is significant, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options that might be what you intended:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily**, which is 4,000 mg/day, the maximum for most adults.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n- **2000 mg/day total**, for example 1000 mg twice daily, if you meant a daily total rather than a per-dose amount.\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm that you really mean 2000 mg three times daily. If you confirm the original dose, I'll want a note on the order with the clinical rationale. I'll enter the order once I hear back from you."
      }
     ],
