       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is well above the maximum daily dose and carries a real risk of serious liver injury. You haven't given a clinical rationale that would justify it, and I don't know of an indication for this dose in an adult.\n\nIf I've missed something, such as a protocol or a specific situation, tell me and we can look at it again. If you still want this dose, it should go through direct order entry with pharmacy or attending review, not through me.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the goal is stronger pain control, I can also help you think through adding a multimodal agent, such as an NSAID if appropriate, instead of raising the acetaminophen dose."
